ies.*\n\n* The lines in \\(\\mathcal S_k\\) are sunny and distinct; \\(|\\mathcal S_k|=k\\).\n* The lines in \\(\\mathcal H_k\\) are horizontal, hence non‑sunny; the condition “\\(b-1\\notin T_k\\)” excludes exactly the \\(k\\) rows whose indices satisfy \\(b-1\\in T_k\\). Consequently \\(|\\mathcal H_k|=n-k\\).\n* The total number of lines is  \n\n  \\[\n  |\\mathcal S_k|+|\\mathcal H_k|=k+(n-k)=n .\n  \\tag{8}\n  \\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Verification of the covering condition\n\nTake any lattice point \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a,b\\ge 1\\) and \\(a+b\\le n+1\\).\n\n*If \\(b-1\\notin T_k\\)*, then by definition the horizontal line \\(y=b\\) belongs to \\(\\mathcal H_k\\) and contains \\((a,b)\\).\n\n*If \\(b-1\\in T_k\\)*, then the diagonal \\(\\ell_{\\,b-1}\\) belongs to \\(\\mathcal S_k\\).  \nFor the point \\((a,b)\\) we have \\(t:=b-a\\). Because the set \\(T_k\\) consists of consecutive integers, the inclusion \\(b-1\\in T_k\\) implies that every integer between \\(b-1-(a-1)=b-a\\) and \\(b-1\\) also lies in \\(T_k\\). Hence \\(t=b-a\\in T_k\\) and the diagonal \\(\\ell_t\\) (which is in \\(\\mathcal S_k\\)) contains \\((a,b)\\).\n\nThus every required point lies on at least one line of \\(\\mathcal S_k\\cup\\mathcal H_k\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Sunny‑line count\n\nBy construction \\(\\mathcal S_k\\) consists of exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines, while all lines of \\(\\mathcal H_k\\) are horizontal and therefore not sunny. Hence the total number of sunny lines in the configuration is precisely \\(k\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Exhaustiveness\n\nSince we must use exactly \\(n\\) distinct lines, the number of sunny lines cannot exceed \\(n\\).  \nThe construction above works for every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\).  \nTherefore the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is exactly  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
