nes can each contain at most one point from each of the \\(n\\) vertical columns, giving at most \\((n-2)n\\) additional points. The total possible coverage is therefore at most \\(2n+(n-2)n=n^2\\), whereas  \n\n   \\[\n   |S_n|=\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}>n^2\\quad\\text{for }n\\ge3,\n   \\]\n\n   a contradiction. Hence no configuration with \\(k\\ge n-1\\) sunny lines can exist.\n\nCombining the explicit constructions (existence for \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\)) with the impossibility proof (non‑existence for \\(k\\ge n-1\\)) yields the complete answer.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{All }k\\text{ with }0\\le k\\le n-2\\text{ are possible, and no other }k\\text{ works}.}\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
